Hi Danni,

Because we lost track of its maintainer, the SemSim package didn't make it
in the current BioC release (BioC 2.3, released in last October).

I can only mention 2 alternatives (maybe there are more, someone on this
list will know better):

   (1) The GOSim package from CRAN. Not officially a BioC package but it
       depends heavily on other BioC packages, especially BioC annotations.

   (2) The GOSemSim package. Only available in BioC devel for now (so you
       will need R-2.9).

 From their Description field, these 2 packages seem to provide functionalities
similar to what SemSim was doing.

